  "concrete_prerequisite_for_exact_rooted_query_test": [
    "A separately reviewed native test receiving entry must obtain the genuine same-publisher signed Main channel and original staged root helper Request, with the actual explicit consent/purpose lifetime intact. It may then acquire the real StockLease and call the real read-only Query directly; StockLease acquisition does not require asserting stock absence, and claimPublication must not be called for this diagnostic.",
    "Add a bounded instance-local negative-only fault checkpoint to the actual tree-capture path after original descriptors are retained, before the constructor can return. It may only force failure/revoke; no caller-supplied successful tree, positive current predicate, UID, signature, Request, stock-absence receipt or arbitrary executable is accepted.",
    "To prove unknown descriptor cleanup rather than an ordinary throwing path alone, the native receiving must cause/observe a real owned-descriptor close failure or unavailable original close receipt and retain that original attempt. A new positive retry, unverified scalar failure flag or statement-order assertion does not establish this.",
    "The actual test assertions should observe Query.start/poll/retired and owning StockLease.retire: after the genuine throwing capture poll remains cleanupPending, retired stays false and no launchctl child is created; repeated calls do not recreate/close a foreign reused descriptor. A successful original capture/close control must retain its genuine positive close flow. These tests are not presently authored or executable through the existing XCTest harness."
  ],
  "smallest_non_authority_software_seam_candidate": {
    "design": "If ordinary-user native behavioral coverage is needed before a genuine Root receiving harness exists, factor the real fixed-tool tree-capture/retirement lifetime into a retained transport-free owner used by Query itself. It owns the actual attempted capture, original tree/partial cleanup receipt and sticky debt; exposes capture/retirement observations only, never a process launch, absence, publication or Request grant. Query must use this same owner at its actual start and final poll cuts; a detached mirror helper is insufficient.",
    "test_use": "Use the existing genuine temporary-directory/native InstallTree fixture to force a real throwing capture (for example a refused child encountered after ancestor capture), and a bounded negative-only descriptor fault to exercise real cleanup debt. Run actual owner capture/retirement with true original FDs, including foreign-number reuse preservation; never set attempted/closed booleans in tests.",
    "boundary": "This would qualify the production cleanup component, not a complete rooted Query run. A separate exact integration assertion/receiving is still required to prove Query uses its original owner. It is a production refactor requiring independent review, not an already available test seam.",
    "status": "PROPOSAL_ONLY_NOT_AUTHORED; no competing source edits requested or made."
  },
